(3806087, 534854, 67145, '<td valign="top">well shawn .. you''ve seriously kicked some butts in this challenge .. <b>congratulations on an excellent photograph and a near pb!!</b> <br/>i was thinking that a chick hatching would go well for this challenge but finding one posed a few problems .. i considered going to the local chicken farm, but felt a bit shy to ask them if i could sit around waiting for an egg to hatch .. (i dont actually know any chicken farms around here but i was assuming there''d be at least one, coz i live in a fairly rural setting ..) <br/>anyway .. enough about chicken farms .. <br/>it appears that your son and your wife are largely responsible for your 4th place in this challenge!!! .. <br/>i dont know why you dont like this image .. it is sooooooo transitions &amp; it tells a story, even tho a bit sad .. lol ...<br/>i particularly like how rhoda''s looking intently at that pie with a sort''v questioning expression .. i''m sure animals, and birds in particular, have more intelligence than we give them credit for .. so you may have to bear a burden of guilt, when you realise from rhoda''s behaviour, that you''ve given her a complex by putting her on that table between the egg and pie ... i reckon it would be totaly obvious to the poor chick the inference there .. i''m hoping rhoda will not be living in fear that she''ll end up in a pie .. altho from her general demeanour i fear it is the case .. :):) .. <br/></td>', 'well shawn .. you''ve seriously kicked some butts in this challenge .. congratulations on an excellent photograph and a near pb!! i was thinking that a chick hatching would go well for this challenge but finding one posed a few problems .. i considered going to the local chicken farm, but felt a bit shy to ask them if i could sit around waiting for an egg to hatch .. (i dont actually know any chicken farms around here but i was assuming there''d be at least one, coz i live in a fairly rural setting ..) anyway .. enough about chicken farms .. it appears that your son and your wife are largely responsible for your 4th place in this challenge!!! .. i dont know why you dont like this image .. it is sooooooo transitions & it tells a story, even tho a bit sad .. lol ...i particularly like how rhoda''s looking intently at that pie with a sort''v questioning expression .. i''m sure animals, and birds in particular, have more intelligence than we give them credit for .. so you may have to bear a burden of guilt, when you realise from rhoda''s behaviour, that you''ve given her a complex by putting her on that table between the egg and pie ... i reckon it would be totaly obvious to the poor chick the inference there .. i''m hoping rhoda will not be living in fear that she''ll end up in a pie .. altho from her general demeanour i fear it is the case .. :):) .. ', '2007-06-20 07:23:59.000000', NULL, 0),
