(3809825, 531185, 68035, '<td valign="top">Nice shot and a good score (top half always worth smiling about).  On the plus side I love the colours you have here, although I would say that it did come across quite noisy on my monitor.  Still doing a lot better than anything I have produced recently</td>', 'Nice shot and a good score (top half always worth smiling about).  On the plus side I love the colours you have here, although I would say that it did come across quite noisy on my monitor.  Still doing a lot better than anything I have produced recently', '2007-06-20 17:18:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3809832, 534779, 74605, '<td valign="top">Fun!  The blue background helps the popcorn "pop"! I like this a lot!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-06-20 23:37:26.</i></td>', 'Fun!  The blue background helps the popcorn "pop"! I like this a lot!', '2007-06-20 17:20:11.000000', '2007-06-21 00:37:26.000000', 0),
(3809858, 534955, 68035, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot and a great title.  So close to another 6 average you must be cursing!!!  Love the composition (but you know how much I love half face shots...although I have never tried one like this before...BTW it works fantastically)<br/> <br/>Plus another one of your great B&amp;W conversions (these seem to be just getting better and better)</td>', 'Lovely shot and a great title.  So close to another 6 average you must be cursing!!!  Love the composition (but you know how much I love half face shots...although I have never tried one like this before...BTW it works fantastically) Plus another one of your great B&W conversions (these seem to be just getting better and better)', '2007-06-20 17:27:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3809870, 535570, 68035, '<td valign="top">Think that you may have really suffered in terms of monitor calibration.  At home this looks bright but OK but on my work pc it came out very very harsh!!!<br/> <br/>Still at least you have the consolation of being in the sudden death match in DPL this week, whilst we languish mid table (and that is only down to my team mates)<br/> <br/>Fortunately I did not enter transitions otherwise no doubt you would have beaten me (AGAIN)</td>', 'Think that you may have really suffered in terms of monitor calibration.  At home this looks bright but OK but on my work pc it came out very very harsh!!! Still at least you have the consolation of being in the sudden death match in DPL this week, whilst we languish mid table (and that is only down to my team mates) Fortunately I did not enter transitions otherwise no doubt you would have beaten me (AGAIN)', '2007-06-20 17:30:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3809919, 531911, 24962, '<td valign="top">Sinister and dramatic, foggy but the detail is still crisp. The conversion fits the shot exactly and increases the atmosphere. I didn''t vote this challenge, but would have scored it a well deserved 9.</td>', 'Sinister and dramatic, foggy but the detail is still crisp. The conversion fits the shot exactly and increases the atmosphere. I didn''t vote this challenge, but would have scored it a well deserved 9.', '2007-06-20 17:42:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3809948, 533901, 53814, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JuliBoc:</b></div><hr/><i>  I love the effect you got with USM. Do you have a formula you use for the different settings? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you Julianne. I have no clue how to sharpen with USM but I think I read somewhere (probably in a DPC forum) that it was best accomplished in several passes of small intensity - one pass after converting from RAW and  the others after final resizing. I prefer to use high pass or edge sharpening, however, neither is legal in basic. (unless the rule has been changed)<br/>Most of the detail in this photo was a result of using an excellent lens and the fact that I backlit with a green light and front lit with daylight. This allowed me to use selective color and curves to combine the textures as I saw fit.</td>', 'Originally posted by JuliBoc:  I love the effect you got with USM. Do you have a formula you use for the different settings?   Thank you Julianne. I have no clue how to sharpen with USM but I think I read somewhere (probably in a DPC forum) that it was best accomplished in several passes of small intensity - one pass after converting from RAW and  the others after final resizing. I prefer to use high pass or edge sharpening, however, neither is legal in basic. (unless the rule has been changed)Most of the detail in this photo was a result of using an excellent lens and the fact that I backlit with a green light and front lit with daylight. This allowed me to use selective color and curves to combine the textures as I saw fit.', '2007-06-20 17:47:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3809969, 533432, 59442, '<td valign="top">..horizontal lines on the petal? I''m not sure what your seeing? It looks ok on every monitor I''ve looked at! :) Thanx for all the comments!</td>', '..horizontal lines on the petal? I''m not sure what your seeing? It looks ok on every monitor I''ve looked at! :) Thanx for all the comments!', '2007-06-20 17:50:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3810000, 531911, 66515, '<td valign="top">Its really good overall and you nearly got a 6 which is pretty darned good. I would have straightened it abit. Granted, the boat was probably tilted in the water but the perception is that its slightly tilted. <br/> <br/>The border could have been removed. The main function of a border is basically to contain the image visually. This shot doesn''t need it. <br/> <br/>That aside, the blue monochrome works really well with it. It definitely has atmosphere and visual appeal.</td>', 'Its really good overall and you nearly got a 6 which is pretty darned good. I would have straightened it abit. Granted, the boat was probably tilted in the water but the perception is that its slightly tilted.  The border could have been removed. The main function of a border is basically to contain the image visually. This shot doesn''t need it.  That aside, the blue monochrome works really well with it. It definitely has atmosphere and visual appeal.', '2007-06-20 17:55:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3810014, 531911, 19952, '<td valign="top">I liked this image a lot, Jack, and gave it a 7. I agree that if the person''s face were clearer, showing him emerging from the fog, this image would have scored even higher. Very nice subject, composition and processing.</td>', 'I liked this image a lot, Jack, and gave it a 7. I agree that if the person''s face were clearer, showing him emerging from the fog, this image would have scored even higher. Very nice subject, composition and processing.', '2007-06-20 17:57:37.000000', NULL, 0),
